{"kind":"request","text":"J4 checker item 3 needs a cleanup ownership decision. At reviewed 77284b97, workspaceFork holds the provider's initial write credential under workspace:\u003cattempt-name\u003e, then sends one revoke. If it cannot confirm, the fork result stays unknown; no judged record names that private cleanup handle and no later operation owes revocation. The fork name is unique per incarnation/hold/opening/attempt; up to three attempts can leave such authority. Its expiry is not established by the fork API. It is never handed to a holder, but the credential remains live until actual revocation or provider expiry. The checker explicitly allows taking this issue to the planner.\n\nA silent retry inside the host or recovery hook would repeat a provider mutation without a recorded operation. Returning a selected fork while setup revocation is uncertain would weaken the current boundary. The small principled repair needs a nonsecret setup-credential handle in a judged cleanup obligation, with a separate revocation operation and private plaintext custody; that extends the hold@2 kernel disposition beyond the two added head/fork rules in adb1a6ed and needs a stated design. An alternative private cleanup outbox would introduce a second durable operation owner outside the existing journal.\n\nPlease choose either (a) a bounded hold@2 cleanup obligation now, with the adopted rule and required ownership/unknown-result behavior, or (b) source landing with this explicit open limit and a separately filed implementation request that owns it. In (b), docs/hosts.md and the implementation note will name that request and will make no cleanup or expiry claim. Other checker repairs and preparation for one final full gate continue independently. No repeat revoke, provider call, deployment or custody read has run for this question.","body":{"conditions":"Decide checker item 3: adopt a concrete cleanup obligation in this head, or explicitly defer it to a named follow-up request with the live setup credential limit documented. This is a design decision, not permission to repeat an unknown provider mutation.","no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8eba6b83351f7a41d9a56e38079c43df6447717c stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0a0b8626cdd726c317fafe42974a68c1cfa2da4b, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:da1ba9e4dfc2ea012511e39a9c3ec5e3be8d2af2","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}